  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is subjected two simple harmonic motions as :<br/>$\\mathrm{x}_1=\\sqrt{7} \\sin 5 \\mathrm{tcm}$ <br/>and $x_2=2 \\sqrt{7} \\sin \\left(5 t+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) \\mathrm{cm}$<br/>where x is displacement and $t$ is time in seconds. The maximum acceleration of the particle is $\\mathrm{x} \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~ms}^{-2}$. The value of x is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$175$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$25 \\sqrt{7}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$5 \\sqrt{7}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$125$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{x}_1=\\sqrt{7} \\sin 5 \\mathrm{t} \\\\ & \\mathrm{x}_2=2 \\sqrt{7} \\sin \\left(5 \\mathrm{t}+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}$<br/>From phasor,<br/><img src=\"assets\\st0003_84f68fbafd05.png\"/><br/>$\\therefore$ Amplitude of resultant $\\mathrm{SHM}=7$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\phi=\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{2 \\sqrt{7} \\times \\sqrt{3} / 2}{\\sqrt{7}+2 \\sqrt{7} \\times \\frac{1}{2}}=\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{2 \\sqrt{7}}=\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ & \\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{R}}=7 \\sin (5 \\mathrm{t}+\\phi) \\\\ & \\quad \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{R}}=-7 \\times 25 \\sin (5 \\mathrm{t}+\\phi) \\\\ & \\therefore \\mathrm{a}_{\\max }=175 \\mathrm{~cm} / \\mathrm{sec}=175 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}